            "ccf:hubmap_id": "HBM789.XTDK.794",
            "rdfs:comment": "This reference organ, Small-intestine-male (https://humanatlas.io/3d-reference-library) was created using data from\nthe Visible Human Male, provided by the National Library of Medicine (Spitzer et al. 1996; Ackerman 1998). The small\nintestines have been updated to include a measurement system. A centerline was made in the center of the intestines,\nand markers were placed along the centerline. The teal discs measure 5 cm along the intestines, the green dashes\nmeasure 1 cm, and the yellow disc marks the jejunoileal junction. The Visible Human Male small intestine total length\nis 285 cm.\n\n**Bibliography:**\n\n* Ackerman, Michael J. 1998. “The Visible Human Project.” *Proceedings of the IEEE* 86 (3): 504–11. https://doi.org/10.1109/5.662875.\n* Spitzer, V., M. J. Ackerman, A. L. Scherzinger, and D. Whitlock. 1996. “The Visible Human Male: A Technical Report.” *Journal of the American Medical Informatics Association* 3 (2): 118–30. https://doi.org/10.1136/jamia.1996.96236280.",
            "dct:title": "3D Reference Organ for Small Intestine, Male",
            "dct:publisher": "HuBMAP",
            "rdfs:label": "3D Reference Organ for Small Intestine, Male",
            "dct:references": [
                "https://doi.org/10.1136/jamia.1996.96236280",
                "https://doi.org/10.1109/5.662875"
            ],
